-- title:
--   Descent of a DVR with invariant uniformiser to the fixed field
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field carrying an action of a finite group $G$ by ring automorphisms, and let $W \subseteq K$ be a valuation subring which is a discrete valuation ring. Assume given $\pi \in K$ with $g \cdot \pi = \pi$ for all $g \in G$ and $\pi \in W$, such that the maximal ideal of $W$ is the principal ideal generated by $\pi$. Assume further the faithfulness hypothesis that for every $g \neq 1$ which preserves $W$ (in the sense $g \cdot x \in W \iff x \in W$ for all $x \in K$) there is $x \in W$ with $g \cdot x - x \notin \mathfrak{m}_W$. Finally let $B$ be a subring of $K$ which is $G$-stable ($b \in B \Rightarrow g \cdot b \in B$) and contained in $W$, and such that $W$ is the localisation of $B$ at the elements of $B$ that are units of $W$: for $f \in K$, $f \in W$ if and only if $f h = g$ for some $g, h \in B$ with $h \notin \mathfrak{m}_W$ whenever $h \in W$. The conclusion has three parts: the valuation subring $W \cap K^G$ of the fixed field, obtained by pulling $W$ back along the inclusion of `FixedPoints.subfield G K`, is a discrete valuation ring; $\pi$, viewed in the fixed field, lies in $W \cap K^G$ and generates its maximal ideal; and for every $G$-invariant $f \in K$ one has $f \in W$ if and only if $f h = g$ for some $g, h \in B$ which are both $G$-invariant and with $h \notin \mathfrak{m}_W$ whenever $h \in W$.
--
--   This is the unramified descent of a discrete valuation ring through a finite group action, together with the descent of a localisation presentation: the invariant subring $W \cap K^G$ is again a discrete valuation ring, the given invariant uniformiser of $W$ remains a uniformiser downstairs (so the extension is unramified with $e = 1$), and the presentation of $W$ as a localisation of $B$ descends to a presentation by invariant numerators and denominators, i.e. by $B^G$. It refines [`ValuationSubring.isDiscreteValuationRing_comap_fixedPoints_and_exists_uniformizer_and_residue_descent`](thm.html#ValuationSubring.isDiscreteValuationRing_comap_fixedPoints_and_exists_uniformizer_and_residue_descent), which it cites, and is used in the construction of charts on quotients of modular curves by finite group actions, where local rings of invariants must be identified as discrete valuation rings with explicit uniformiser and explicit fractions.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ValuationSubring_maximalIdeal_comap_fixedPoints_eq_span_and_mem_iff_exists_invariant_of_isLocalization.lean

